# Candidate minimal x4 repair: replace only the first final-compression
# FastTwoSum with TwoSum. No magnitude ordering is assumed for b/a1/a2/a3.
# If this proves, the final renormalization network is structurally valid even
# under destructive cancellation that reorders the pre-compression terms.

variable b
variable a1
variable a2
variable a3

# w0, w1 = two_sum(b, a1)          # repaired operation
# w1, w2 = two_sum(w1, a2)
# w2, w3 = two_sum(w2, a3)
# z0, rho = two_sum(w0, w1)
# z1, sigma = two_sum(rho, w2)
# z2, z3 = fast_two_sum(sigma, w3)
two_sum      b a1
two_sum      a1 a2
two_sum      a2 a3
two_sum      b a1
two_sum      a1 a2
fast_two_sum a2 a3

prove b strongly_dominates a1
prove a1 strongly_dominates a2
prove a2 strongly_dominates a3
